WEBVTT

01:30.520 --> 01:33.480
Episode 4: 
Mind of a Lone Wolf

01:32.190 --> 01:36.160
So basically, Sakagami was 
trying to get to a driving school.

01:38.530 --> 01:41.620
Hang on. Just because
 he took the pickup bus,

01:41.620 --> 01:44.500
that doesn't mean he was 
going to the driving school.

01:44.500 --> 01:48.040
He may have just caught it 'cause 
it's a convenient way to get around.

01:50.000 --> 01:55.800
But the driving school wouldn't let someone
 on if they aren't enrolled, would they?

01:55.800 --> 01:57.680
How would they know he wasn't?

02:03.310 --> 02:04.350
His bag.

02:04.350 --> 02:07.480
Wait, no, it was a folder.

02:07.770 --> 02:11.310
I see. Now that you mention it, 
I've seen that before.

02:11.860 --> 02:16.280
Someone getting on a bus 
holding a white folder.

02:16.740 --> 02:21.120
That means Sakagami is 
trying to get his driver's license.

02:21.870 --> 02:23.120
But what for?

02:23.530 --> 02:28.160
Or we can also ask, 
what does he plan to use his license for?

02:28.830 --> 02:31.040
What would it enable him to do?

02:31.670 --> 02:32.750
Photo ID?

02:33.210 --> 02:34.420
Birth date?

02:34.840 --> 02:35.840
Address?

02:36.670 --> 02:43.680
In other words, I'm thinking about the
 secondary use of a driver's license as ID.

02:46.100 --> 02:49.810
Why does Sakagami want a driver's license?

02:50.390 --> 02:53.940
One: to gain the right to drive.

02:54.270 --> 02:57.400
Two: to gain identification.

02:57.860 --> 03:00.700
Is there a third or a fourth?

03:02.570 --> 03:05.450
It would have to be the first, clearly.

03:05.740 --> 03:09.830
More often than not, when someone
 says something is clear, it isn't.

03:11.420 --> 03:17.300
Something tells me he isn't <i>just</i>
trying to get his driver's license.

03:32.270 --> 03:34.360
I have three questions.

03:35.360 --> 03:43.490
Kira West Driving School

03:35.360 --> 03:43.490
Distance

03:35.360 --> 03:43.490
Age

03:36.610 --> 03:39.570
First: the distance.

03:39.900 --> 03:43.490
Why did Sakagami choose 
Kira North Driving School?

03:43.490 --> 03:55.130
Kira West Driving School

03:43.490 --> 03:55.130
Distance

03:43.490 --> 03:55.130
Age

03:43.490 --> 03:55.130
Disposition

03:43.860 --> 03:46.700
Kira North Driving School 
is on the outskirts of town.

03:46.700 --> 03:50.580
If I remember correctly, 
on the day he stole Osanai's bike,

03:50.580 --> 03:54.210
he mentioned something 
about going back to get his own.

03:55.130 --> 03:57.540
That means he's been walking to school.

03:58.050 --> 04:00.300
His home is near Minakami High School.

04:00.630 --> 04:05.140
Minakami High School is, roughly speaking, 
on the southwest side of town.

04:05.510 --> 04:09.140
Getting from his home to 
Kira North Driving School

04:09.140 --> 04:12.020
would've been a pain for him, 
even with taking the bus.

04:12.810 --> 04:19.020
And as I'm sure you're aware, 
there's another driving school.

04:19.020 --> 04:22.530
Kira West Driving School

04:19.020 --> 04:22.530
Distance

04:20.150 --> 04:22.150
Kira West Driving School.

04:23.530 --> 04:27.200
Which is just north 
of Minakami High School.

04:27.200 --> 04:28.120
Right.

04:28.120 --> 04:32.000
Kira West Driving School

04:28.120 --> 04:32.000
Distance

04:28.120 --> 04:32.000
Age

04:28.120 --> 04:32.000
Disposition

04:28.370 --> 04:32.000
In other words, 
not very far from Sakagami's place.

04:32.330 --> 04:36.460
If you think about access, 
Kira West would be the clear choice.

04:37.040 --> 04:40.920
"More often than not, when someone
 says something is clear, it isn't."

04:40.920 --> 04:42.840
A trite comeback.

04:42.840 --> 04:46.090
But if you find the point weak,

04:43.760 --> 04:47.760
Kira West Driving School

04:43.760 --> 04:47.760
Distance

04:43.760 --> 04:47.760
Age

04:43.760 --> 04:47.760
Disposition

04:46.090 --> 04:51.560
would you mind scoring 
how suspicious you think it is? As a ratio.

04:51.560 --> 04:52.770
A ratio?

04:56.060 --> 04:59.770
I'd say it's unsuspicious 
by a ratio of 6.5:3.5.

04:59.770 --> 05:01.570
That's pretty significant.

05:02.150 --> 05:03.570
Okay, next.

05:02.780 --> 05:05.650
Age

05:04.030 --> 05:05.200
His age.

05:05.650 --> 05:09.740
Sakagami called one of the 
people in his group "Senpai."

05:05.650 --> 05:14.040
Kira West Driving School

05:05.650 --> 05:14.040
Distance

05:05.650 --> 05:14.040
Age

05:05.650 --> 05:14.040
Disposition

05:10.200 --> 05:14.620
And that senpai used the 
same honorific with another member.

05:15.080 --> 05:16.290
What's your point?

05:16.870 --> 05:21.750
If his senpai has a senpai,
that means Sakagami is a junior of a junior.

05:22.300 --> 05:27.430
In other words, barring very 
unusual circumstances, he's a first-year.

05:28.590 --> 05:31.720
I see. A first-year in high school.

05:31.720 --> 05:32.850
And we're...

05:33.680 --> 05:36.310
Yes, 15 or 16.

05:36.890 --> 05:42.190
The first licenses you can get 
are for mopeds and motorcycles.

05:42.190 --> 05:43.980
And only from 16.

05:44.570 --> 05:46.780
It's June right now.

05:47.450 --> 05:50.870
Roughly five in six first-years are still 15.

05:51.240 --> 05:53.580
And at 15, you can't get a license.

05:53.580 --> 05:58.620
Which means it's unsuspicious 
by a ratio of 1:5. Do you follow?

05:59.710 --> 06:02.840
Disposition

06:00.250 --> 06:02.840
Third: his disposition.

06:02.840 --> 06:06.670
Kira West Driving School

06:02.840 --> 06:06.670
Distance

06:02.840 --> 06:06.670
Age

06:02.840 --> 06:06.670
Disposition

06:03.170 --> 06:05.760
Let's suppose he's 16.

06:05.760 --> 06:13.310
Now, Sakagami-kun, who had the nerve 
to steal a bike, was late for driving school.

06:13.890 --> 06:16.350
The pickup bus had already left.

06:16.350 --> 06:19.770
The only way he could catch up
 was to bike to the next stop.

06:19.770 --> 06:22.980
Now, do you really think 
he would be that desperate?

06:22.980 --> 06:24.570
I might, if I were him.

06:24.570 --> 06:26.940
The question is whether Sakagami would be.

06:28.200 --> 06:30.070
Kira West Driving School

06:28.200 --> 06:30.070
Distance

06:28.200 --> 06:30.070
Age

06:28.200 --> 06:30.070
Disposition

06:28.200 --> 06:30.070
Why didn't he just skip that day?

06:31.240 --> 06:34.330
Maybe he was in a hurry 
to get his license for some reason.

06:34.330 --> 06:35.660
What reason would that be?

06:36.330 --> 06:38.620
Here's the simple solution:

06:38.620 --> 06:43.710
Someone else is making him get his license.

06:43.710 --> 06:45.210
Someone else?

06:45.880 --> 06:47.920
But what good would it do them?

06:48.510 --> 06:50.220
Well, who can say?

06:50.760 --> 06:53.680
Either way, I want you to evaluate

06:53.680 --> 06:58.350
whether it's suspicious how serious 
this bike thief is about getting his license?

07:01.350 --> 07:02.690
Let me think.

07:03.360 --> 07:05.520
Unsuspicious by 7:3.

07:07.070 --> 07:13.370
Okay, let's try calculating 
how suspicious you think it is.

07:14.870 --> 07:19.910
First, you trusted Sakagami 
had his reasons by a ratio of 65%.

07:20.370 --> 07:24.420
Then, you said 1:5, which is 17%.

07:24.920 --> 07:27.460
The third number was 70%.

07:28.050 --> 07:28.920
Kengo.

07:29.340 --> 07:36.260
By what ratio would you say you really
 believe he's <i>just</i> trying to get his license?

07:38.680 --> 07:40.390
It's 0.077.

07:40.390 --> 07:42.190
Roughly 8%.

07:43.350 --> 07:48.400
In other words, you're 92%
suspicious of Sakagami's reasons.

07:48.400 --> 07:50.070
Are you convinced now?

07:50.570 --> 07:51.570
Damn it.

07:52.200 --> 07:55.160
You've always been like this.

07:55.530 --> 07:58.330
You really are a little shit.

07:58.700 --> 08:01.660
For now, I'll take that as a compliment.

08:02.580 --> 08:07.840
In any case, there <i>is</i> something dubious 
about him just trying to get his license.

08:10.090 --> 08:16.600
Now, if you were going to use a driver's license
 for something nefarious, what would it be?

08:17.550 --> 08:22.480
The first thing that springs to mind 
on abusing ID is organized crime.

08:23.060 --> 08:25.190
In an extreme case.

08:25.730 --> 08:27.860
But I'm not sure it's that.

08:28.190 --> 08:31.940
Sakagami doesn't seem 
like a big-shot underling.

08:31.940 --> 08:35.740
"Big-shot underling" has a weird ring to it.

08:36.320 --> 08:42.000
So what could our Sakagami accomplish 
by having a driver's license?

08:44.460 --> 08:47.880
I think it's most likely a cheap way
 of earning some pocket change.

08:47.880 --> 08:49.260
Sounds about right.

08:49.260 --> 08:50.880
You're convinced?

08:51.420 --> 08:56.090
I'd be more surprised if someone of his sort
 had any motivation besides money.

08:57.300 --> 09:02.520
But listen, Jogoro, 
I'm starting to have my doubts.

09:03.680 --> 09:06.520
Supposing he <i>does</i> want 
to abuse his driver's license,

09:06.520 --> 09:08.770
it's still a 16-year-old's license.

09:09.150 --> 09:10.650
What use would it have?

09:10.650 --> 09:15.400
You're right. You can't move much money
with a 16-year-old's license.

09:15.860 --> 09:19.910
Besides, it would defeat the purpose
 if it was his own license.

09:20.740 --> 09:22.120
Which means...

09:22.700 --> 09:25.660
If he wants to make 
proper spending money,

09:25.660 --> 09:29.710
he'd need to get his license using 
the name of someone who's at least 18.

09:30.290 --> 09:32.340
Hang on, Jogoro.

09:32.340 --> 09:34.670
Do you know what you're suggesting?

09:35.090 --> 09:38.840
That's the very definition of forgery.

09:40.680 --> 09:43.180
<b>What to bring when enrolling</b>

09:43.720 --> 09:45.680
<b>The applicant's certificate of residence, seal, identification...</b>

09:46.270 --> 09:51.020
If memory serves, all you need to 
earn a certificate of residence is a seal,

09:51.020 --> 09:54.150
a health insurance card, 
and one more public document.

09:55.030 --> 09:58.240
All you'd need to do is to choose 
someone to steal those things from.

09:58.240 --> 10:01.870
Someone over 18 who has 
a residence in this town.

10:01.870 --> 10:04.580
Someone who doesn't 
have a driver's license yet.

10:07.330 --> 10:10.920
And you don't need 
more than just a basic seal.

10:11.340 --> 10:14.800
You could easily buy a seal for a name 
like "Sato" at a stationery shop.

10:19.260 --> 10:24.890
The group that's using Sakagami would 
probably choose a pretty rare last name.

10:25.350 --> 10:29.230
Iokibe

10:25.850 --> 10:29.230
There's a student named 
Iokibe-san in this town.

10:29.520 --> 10:30.650
Iokibe?

10:31.060 --> 10:36.610
Iokibe-san was at the polls 
when a burglar entered his home.

10:37.320 --> 10:40.860
In other words, he's of voting age.

10:40.860 --> 10:44.580
So he's over 18, lives in this town,

10:44.580 --> 10:50.420
and the bike Sakagami stole
 was found near his place.

10:51.170 --> 10:54.340
I think that goes beyond 
being a coincidence.

10:54.670 --> 10:55.710
I see.

10:56.460 --> 10:59.010
But there's still no evidence.

10:59.340 --> 11:04.600
Age

10:59.340 --> 11:04.600
Disposition

10:59.340 --> 11:04.600
Kira West Driving School

10:59.340 --> 11:04.600
Distance

10:59.840 --> 11:01.050
You're right.

11:07.520 --> 11:09.100
I've finally got it.

11:09.980 --> 11:12.730
I'll put it simply.

11:13.270 --> 11:17.990
Osanai-san is up against a group 
that's attempting to commit fraud.

11:18.940 --> 11:20.030
What?

11:22.950 --> 11:26.580
Sakagami stole Osanai-san's bike,

11:26.580 --> 11:31.000
destroyed it, and worst of all, 
ruined her strawberry tart.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.330
She won't let that slide.

11:32.750 --> 11:37.550
Three days ago, when we learned
Sakagami was going to driving school,

11:37.550 --> 11:39.430
Osanai-san said:

11:40.260 --> 11:42.430
We finally caught him.

11:42.680 --> 11:45.600
Osanai-san is sensitive 
to Sakagami's actions.

11:45.600 --> 11:48.850
She'd tear his windpipe out 
with her teeth given the chance.

11:48.850 --> 11:50.060
Just a second.

11:51.850 --> 11:55.980
When you say Osanai, 
you mean <i>that</i> Osanai, right?

11:55.980 --> 11:57.650
The, uh, well...

11:58.280 --> 12:01.200
The embodiment of shyness.

12:01.990 --> 12:04.570
Yeah. That Osanai Yuki.

12:04.990 --> 12:08.040
And you're saying 
she'd rip out his windpipe?

12:08.040 --> 12:09.700
No, Kengo.

12:10.830 --> 12:12.830
I used to be clever.

12:13.250 --> 12:16.590
My aspiration is to be ordinary 
because I got tired of it.

12:17.750 --> 12:19.880
I want you to keep this a secret.

12:21.300 --> 12:23.220
Osanai-san's the same.

12:23.840 --> 12:28.600
But what Osanai-san's trying 
to abandon isn't her cleverness.

12:29.430 --> 12:34.900
If I was a fox, she used to be a wolf.

12:37.480 --> 12:41.360
Nowadays, she really only ever 
shows any kind of happiness

12:41.360 --> 12:44.200
when there's something sweet in front of her.

12:44.200 --> 12:46.950
But she wasn't like that before.

12:47.950 --> 12:55.580
Osanai-san showed the most joy while
beating those who had done her harm to a pulp.

12:56.420 --> 13:00.090
Nope. I'm not believing that.
 Not until I've seen it for myself.

13:02.170 --> 13:06.140
Anyway, Osanai-san is getting close
 to some dangerous people.

13:06.760 --> 13:09.510
And they are, no doubt, men.

13:10.180 --> 13:16.270
If devious men were to capture Osanai-san,
 how would they treat her?

13:22.610 --> 13:25.030
There's something we can confirm right away.

13:26.910 --> 13:29.120
Hey. Do you have a minute?

13:29.780 --> 13:34.500
I want to know the birth date of
a Minakami High first-year named Sakagami.

13:38.710 --> 13:41.420
That's right. I'll leave you to decide how.

13:42.630 --> 13:44.050
No, not really.

13:44.970 --> 13:47.470
Yeah. It's a Kobato thing.

13:50.180 --> 13:51.180
What?

13:51.850 --> 13:54.100
And you accepted that?

13:55.230 --> 13:57.560
No, it's fine.

13:58.150 --> 13:59.610
Did you find out?

14:01.070 --> 14:03.480
Yeah. That's all I need.

14:03.480 --> 14:05.570
Bye. Thanks for the help.

14:07.280 --> 14:09.070
She got there ahead of us.

14:09.070 --> 14:10.280
To Sakagami?

14:10.280 --> 14:11.580
Who was that, anyway?

14:11.580 --> 14:12.740
My sister.

14:13.330 --> 14:16.210
Osanai already asked her the same thing.

14:17.870 --> 14:22.380
I didn't know they were on such good terms.

14:22.880 --> 14:26.840
Well, by my sister's standards, 
if you talk to her, you're already friends.

14:27.340 --> 14:30.090
You came to our house, 
so you're practically best friends.

14:31.300 --> 14:33.890
Anyway, I have your answer.

14:34.970 --> 14:37.140
There's only one guy
with the last name "Sakagami."

14:37.600 --> 14:41.440
She'd forgotten what date it was,
 but he was born in December.

14:42.020 --> 14:45.030
At the very least, 
we now know Sakagami's definitely 15.

14:49.030 --> 14:50.360
It's from Osanai-san.

14:51.320 --> 14:52.280
What is it?

14:52.780 --> 14:54.450
Uh, I don't know.

14:56.120 --> 14:58.620
Message unsent

14:58.910 --> 15:04.000
Do you think someone might have stopped her 
from trying to send an incriminating photo?

15:09.260 --> 15:14.260
Kira West Driving School

15:09.260 --> 15:14.260
Distance

15:09.260 --> 15:14.260
Age

15:09.260 --> 15:14.260
Disposition

15:26.940 --> 15:28.650
Kengo, what time is it?

15:29.990 --> 15:31.450
Four twenty.

15:32.780 --> 15:33.820
It's coming.

15:48.550 --> 15:48.920
<b>Driving School</b>

15:48.920 --> 15:49.090
<b>Driving School</b>

15:49.090 --> 15:49.460
<b>Driving School</b>

15:49.460 --> 15:50.300
<b>Driving School</b>

15:50.300 --> 15:53.720
Jogoro. What's wrong with you?

15:59.060 --> 16:02.060
<b>Kira North Driving School</b>

16:06.520 --> 16:09.280
<b>Kira North Driving School</b>

16:38.180 --> 16:41.430
You didn't need to come here in such a hurry.

16:42.230 --> 16:43.440
Osanai?

16:43.810 --> 16:44.810
That's her?

16:47.440 --> 16:49.900
Why is Dojima-kun here with you?

16:50.320 --> 16:54.570
Why? I wouldn't be able to handle 
a dangerous situation on my own.

16:54.950 --> 16:56.660
Dangerous?

16:56.660 --> 16:58.490
You followed Sakagami here, didn't you?

16:58.990 --> 17:00.540
I did.

17:01.080 --> 17:02.710
Didn't you call for help?

17:02.710 --> 17:04.960
I never did such a thing.

17:04.960 --> 17:06.080
It's just...

17:06.420 --> 17:09.420
I thought someone might have 
forced you to unsend your message.

17:10.920 --> 17:13.840
I just sent the wrong photo.

17:13.840 --> 17:16.220
I tried to resend it,

17:16.740 --> 17:18.600
but it didn't go through.

17:18.600 --> 17:20.850
I guess the signal isn't too good here.

17:24.230 --> 17:28.980
Photo evidence that Sakagami-san 
enrolled under Iokibe-san's name.

17:30.730 --> 17:33.610
I see. Thank goodness.

17:33.610 --> 17:36.490
But I mean, you didn't 
pick up your phone at all.

17:36.490 --> 17:42.200
I turned it off. In case someone 
suspected me of taking sneak shots.

17:45.710 --> 17:47.120
Um...

17:47.830 --> 17:52.710
Kengo, Osanai-san says 
she's already completed her mission.

17:52.710 --> 17:55.840
Uh, okay. I'm glad for you.

17:56.930 --> 17:58.340
But are you <i>really</i> Osanai?

18:01.560 --> 18:03.270
Nice to meet you.

18:03.270 --> 18:06.600
I'm Yuki's twin sister, Maki.

18:13.360 --> 18:16.280
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

18:18.530 --> 18:22.790
<b>Kira: Five high school students arrested</b>

18:18.530 --> 18:22.790
<b>for reselling high-value tickets using fraudulent licenses</b>

18:25.250 --> 18:26.870
I've gone and done it.

18:27.540 --> 18:29.420
You sure have.

18:30.250 --> 18:32.960
Sakagami was being used.

18:32.960 --> 18:37.010
He was planning on getting a motorcycle 
license once he got into high school.

18:37.510 --> 18:39.510
He mentioned that to the group,

18:39.510 --> 18:42.930
and they forced him to go to driving 
school under someone else's name.

18:42.930 --> 18:45.060
And now, he has a criminal record.

18:46.020 --> 18:47.890
It sucks for people at the bottom, huh?

18:47.890 --> 18:51.060
I feel sorry for Iokibe-san.

18:51.060 --> 18:51.810
Yeah.

18:51.810 --> 18:56.610
All because the group found out 
he doesn't have a license.

18:56.610 --> 19:01.200
But we weren't the ones 
who ratted them out directly.

19:01.200 --> 19:05.840
We simply made an anonymous 
warning to a café in town.

19:06.040 --> 19:10.750
That someone named Iokibe 
might be up to something bad.

19:11.210 --> 19:13.880
And we provided photo 
evidence for good measure.

19:15.590 --> 19:19.010
They were the ones who were 
reselling concert tickets at high prices.

19:19.550 --> 19:21.110
I know, but...

19:21.110 --> 19:24.740
I get it. It's not exactly a good feeling.

19:26.260 --> 19:28.980
I decided I wouldn't do it anymore.

19:29.450 --> 19:32.680
I decided I would become an ordinary person.

19:33.540 --> 19:35.630
I'm sorry, Kobato-kun.

19:35.630 --> 19:38.730
You tried to stop me, just as you promised.

19:40.550 --> 19:42.910
I broke my promise, too.

19:43.350 --> 19:46.230
I decided I wouldn't 
play detective anymore.

19:46.230 --> 19:48.000
And thinking back...

19:48.510 --> 19:49.490
The pochette.

19:50.010 --> 19:51.260
The delicious hot cocoa.

19:51.710 --> 19:53.490
The broken vase.

19:53.880 --> 19:55.500
That's three times now.

19:56.610 --> 19:58.490
That's a lot of strikes.

19:59.250 --> 20:00.770
For both of us.

20:07.240 --> 20:08.280
Wanna call it quits?

20:09.790 --> 20:12.300
I'm persistent. It's who I am.

20:12.300 --> 20:14.930
You're nosy. That's you.

20:14.930 --> 20:19.290
Maybe we should just accept 
that's just the way we are.

20:21.450 --> 20:23.150
We're giving up?

20:23.150 --> 20:26.590
I mean, we always end up messing up.

20:28.720 --> 20:35.660
I know you're discouraged, 
but we're trying to fix our flaws, Osanai-san.

20:35.660 --> 20:37.160
It won't always be easy.

20:38.470 --> 20:39.810
Let's keep going.

20:39.810 --> 20:42.330
No need to give up. We can take our time.

21:15.960 --> 21:17.960
<b>Concubine</b>

